    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d613">

                <pb facs="0576" n="500" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/17587a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Consul Simpich </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-22T14:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 22, 1916, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Ascertain and telegraph number and location infantry, cavalry and artillery
                    forces now in northwestern part of Sonora; also number cannon. Keep Department
                    informed of all changes in troop movements in said section as quickly as they
                    occur.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
